Non-cursed unihorns have a random chance to fix one or more problems.
Blessed unihorns are more likely to fix something per attempt, and
fix more problems per attempt on average, than uncursed horns.

So:
    1) Yes, keep the horn blessed -- not only does it work better, but
once you get to the stage of the game where your stuff gets randomly
cursed, it takes two curses hitting your unihorn before it becomes a
menace.

    2) When you need to use it, keep (a)pplying it until all your
status afflications are gone. There is a random factor, so don't give
up just because it doesn't completely fix all your problems (or even
any of your problems) on the first go.

    3) Watch messages carefully. There is a world of difference between
"Nothing happens" and "Nothing seems to happen."

    4) When fighting something that can afflict you with statusline
problems, it can attack you again and re-inflict a problem you just
fixed. Again, close attenion and keep trying with the unihorn.

Fixable troubles, in order, are: sick, blind, hallucinating, vomiting,
confused and stunned. Odds, from a comment in src/apply.c:
         *              Chances for number of troubles to be fixed
         *               0      1      2      3      4      5      6      7
         *   blessed:  22.7%  22.7%  19.5%  15.4%  10.7%   5.7%   2.6%   0.8%
         *  uncursed:  35.4%  35.4%  22.9%   6.3%    0      0      0      0

